# Series to keep refreshed by refresh-library.sh — one URL per line.
# Blank lines and anything after a # are ignored. Paste the same series URLs
# you'd hand to `tomo` directly. Tomo only downloads chapters you don't have yet.
#
# After the URL you can list the weekday(s) the series usually updates
# (mon tue wed thu fri sat sun, comma-separated) — then a daily cron run only
# checks it on those days. No tag (or "daily") means check every run.
# FORCE_ALL=1 ./refresh-library.sh ignores the tags when you want a full pass.
#
# After the days you can add a series name override (spaces allowed) — it's
# passed to `tomo -name` so the folder/file naming stays stable when a source
# titles the series differently from the library folder you already have.
# A name requires a days field before it (use "daily" if there's no fixed day).

# https://mangadex.org/title/<id>/<slug>            wed        # weekly, Wednesdays
# https://asuracomics.com/series/<slug>             tue,sat    # twice a week
# https://weebcentral.com/series/<id>/<slug>                   # irregular → every run
# https://weebcentral.com/series/<id>/Sousou-no-Frieren  tue  Sousou no Frieren   # keep MangaDex-era folder name
